# D-93 with A3 (Codex, 2026-09-28).  The host calls its own capturing model before the return: an ordinary
# (M, M) call over the model's occurrence, its capture n the hidden input the host supplies -- the host's value
# at the call; no node is built for the call.  makeAdder 5: q = addN(1) with n 5 = 6; n becomes 15; r = addN(1)
# with n 15 = 16; n becomes q + r = 22; the returned node carries n 22: add(1) = 23.  The base translator
# refused ("a callable merge host names a nested method outside the return").  Entry 7.
fn: makeAdder (int: n) fn: (int: x) int
    fn: addN (int: x) int
        return: n + x
    int: q (addN: 1)
    n: n + 10
    int: r (addN: 1)
    n: q + r
    return: addN

add: makeAdder 5
int: a (add: 1)
int: ok 0
if: a = 23
    ok: 7
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: ok; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
